<!--
    The app's default (English) strings. Persian lives in values-fa/.

    It used to be the other way round: the locale was pinned to fa:IR, resConfigs kept only
    "en", and so this file held Persian and every language folder was stripped. Language is a
    setting now (see TextoLocale), resConfigs keeps "en" and "fa", and Android resolves the
    two folders the ordinary way.

    Both files carry the same keys. A key defined here and missing there falls back to
    English mid-sentence, which is worse than either language on its own.
-->
